n $[0,5]$ because this interval contains points where the function is not defined. In particular, it is not defined at $x=0.$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176605 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176605 #edb/ref 1061 12791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176605 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9ff3fa5a-39c6-574d-bfa0-7e467bf44083" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176605 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176606 #edb/ref 1061 12792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176606 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8c5c661d-87d1-5fdd-b4cf-9b1217993d69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176606 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176607 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176607 #edb/ref 1061 12794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176607 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3001b2d1-c302-5b15-b3a6-3ff0fa36821e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176607 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176608 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176608 #edb/ref 1061 12795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7889a404-286a-5541-b477-ed0966b909de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176655 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176655 #edb/ref 1061 217080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176655 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a9620c91-7f1f-5c90-81f9-15b63580b9b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176655 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176656 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176656 #edb/ref 1061 217081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176656 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7c94f745-4162-5e7d-841a-0a7d3f00e84a" #edb/r